## Server Setup

The server exposes a FastAPI application and runs in two Docker containers: one for the Python app, one for PostgreSQL. Database data is persisted at `/var/lib/postgresql/data`.

**Live server:** `http://76.13.171.142:8000`  
SSH access: contact Lorenzo for credentials.

### Deploy with Docker

```bash
git clone https://github.com/LorenzoBicalho/TCC.git
cd server
# Create environment file (use .env.example as reference)
nano .env
# Install Docker tooling
pip install docker docker-compose
# Build and start containers
docker-compose up --build
```

**Useful Docker commands:**
```bash
docker ps -a                            # List all containers
docker logs <container_name>            # View container logs
docker exec -it <container_name> sh     # Open a shell inside a container
```

---

### Run Locally (no Docker)

```bash
git clone https://github.com/LorenzoBicalho/TCC.git
cd server
# Create environment file (use .env.example as reference)
nano .env
# Create and activate a virtual environment
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
# Run on localhost only
uvicorn main:app --reload
# Run on all interfaces (visible to other devices on the LAN)
uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload
```

---

### Initialize the Global Model

Insert the first global model (version 1) before any client can interact with the server:

```bash
cd script
python script.py --init load --force
```

---

### Database Migrations

Generate a migration whenever you change a database schema:

```bash
cd server/db
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "<description of change>"
alembic upgrade head
```

Apply the migration:

```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

If running inside Docker containers, restart them instead:

```bash
docker-compose down
docker-compose up --build
```

---

### Inspect the Database

**Locally:** Install [pgAdmin 4](https://www.pgadmin.org/) (or any PostgreSQL client) and connect using the credentials in your `.env` file. Example queries are available in `server/db/queries/`.

**On the remote server:** Connect via SSH and use `psql` inside the database container:

```bash
docker exec -it <db_container_name> psql -U <db_user> -d <db_name>
```

---

## Mock Client (Testing)

The mock client simulates a Raspberry Pi device. All scripts are in the `mock_client/` directory.

```bash
cd mock_client
```

### Arguments Reference

| Argument | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--request` | ✅ | Endpoint to call: `clients` or `weights` |
| `--client` | ✅ | Client letter A–J (maps to `mock_client_<letter>`) |
| `--base-url` | | Server base URL (default: `http://127.0.0.1:8000`) |
| `--description` | | Optional description, only with `--request clients` |
| `--version` | | Model version to send (only with `--request weights`, no `--train`) |
| `--train` | | Run full train + push flow (only with `--request weights`) |
| `--samples` | | Number of training samples (default: 1600, used with `--train`) |
| `--seed` | | Random seed for reproducibility |
| `--rounds` | | Number of pull → train → push rounds (default: 1) |
| `--storegbl` | | Also evaluate global model on full CSV (used with `--train`) |
| `--alpha` | | Learning rate (default: 0.01) |
| `--epochs` | | Training epochs (default: 2) |
| `--shuffle` | | Shuffle data before training |
| `--grad-clip` | | Gradient clipping threshold |
| `--mu` | | FedProx mu regularization parameter (default: 0.0) |

### Examples

**Register a client** (`POST /clients`):

```bash
# Against local server
python3 client.py --request clients --client D
# Against remote server
python3 client.py --base-url http://76.13.171.142:8000 --request clients --client D
```

**Submit dummy weights** (`POST /weights`, no training):

```bash
python3 client.py --request weights --client D --version 1
```

**Full federated round** (pull global model → train on local data → push weights):

```bash
python3 client.py --request weights --train --client D --samples 1600
```

**Full round with extra options** (2 rounds, reproducible, evaluate global model):

```bash
python3 client.py \
  --request weights --train \
  --client D --samples 1600 \
  --rounds 2 --seed 42 \
  --epochs 5 --alpha 0.005 \
  --shuffle --storegbl
```

